From 78fc5f4ba249cc542ed8a51f2c40a7640faad259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T4890 (a): a shared pronoun no longer counts as a shared
 field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The founder's thread 51037: „GEC (his firm) has an office in Almaty" recalled
another contact's need, „Rebut (his startup) … looking for users and
pilots". The only word the two shared was „his". 2608's recall now rests
only on words of four letters or more. At three letters, a word is far more
often a pronoun or a joining word (his, and, has) than a trade. The 2608
case (საწყობი) still matches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
---
 src/services/__tests__/needRecall.test.ts | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 src/services/needRecall.ts                | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

